From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wu Yu Wei <yuweiwu@pm.me>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 15:44:31 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Size the font optically

CSS font-optical-sizing: auto sets a font's opsz axis to the font size.
StyleProperty::OpticalSizing (TextStyle::optical_sizing, off by default,
as upstream has it) asks for it: the shaper puts opsz at the item's font
size before the item's own variations, which win where they set it, so
a font with the axis is shaped, and its run's coordinates are taken, at
that size; a font without the axis ignores it.

Items split where it changes, and the kept shapings tell layouts with
and without it apart (RunStyle).
